    "review-finding-1.json": {"sha256": "53927ab1c0c316b0f5b9a0f14d8a36434cc94a7a94a4a7dd3e2195a1fe47343e", "bytes": 1086, "preserved": {"requirement": "REQ-REV-003/015; AI secret-exposure controls; NFR-PRV-001", "severity": "HIGH", "blocks": true, "owner": "gateway", "reviewer": "independent-review", "description": "Secret screening misses quoted JSON credential assignments, encrypted private-key markers and NFKC token representations. At src/server/src/ai/gateway/index.ts:28-31, the credential regex does not allow the JSON label's closing quote, encrypted PEM is omitted, and redaction uses original rather than normalized text. Both independent reviewers reproduced dispatch of synthetic examples with mocked Prisma/transport and no external calls. Reject high-confidence credential/private-key representations before attempts, consistently screen/redact normalized lower-confidence tokens without rewriting grounding IDs, and add adversarial cases across narrative, diff, criterion and evidence fields. Live provider mode remains disabled; no real credential disclosure is claimed.", "evidence": ["src/server/src/ai/gateway/index.ts", "src/server/test/ai-gateway.spec.ts"]}, "kind": "finding request"},
    "review-finding-2.json": {"sha256": "694039c30eb2730f5edc1a4cfa0d555b4e0baa0884d6b284623484b20e87cfba", "bytes": 867, "preserved": {"requirement": "REQ-REV-014; AI transport body/deadline/resource bounds", "severity": "MEDIUM", "blocks": true, "owner": "gateway", "reviewer": "independent-review", "description": "An oversized advertised Content-Length is rejected at transport.ts:41-42 before the body reader is acquired. Finally at lines61-63 clears timer/removes the deadline listener without aborting or cancelling the unread body. Both independent synthetic open-stream probes returned INVALID_OUTPUT while bodyCancelled=false and transportSignalAborted=false. Abort/cancel every early transport rejection with bounded cleanup; verify advertised and actual overflow, invalid UTF-8, and deadline during reads leave no live body. No real network call was made.", "evidence": ["src/server/src/ai/gateway/transport.ts", "src/server/test/ai-gateway.spec.ts"]}, "kind": "finding request"},
    "review-finding-3.json": {"sha256": "8858d94f0af7e18ba7151abdb5371fc39e1202e1e494bd73a95d8c703d3d2428", "bytes": 891, "preserved": {"requirement": "NFR-OBS-001; NFR-RES-001; safe provider usage accounting", "severity": "MEDIUM", "blocks": true, "owner": "gateway", "reviewer": "independent-review", "description": "decode in gateway/index.ts:92-100 validates advisory content before returning envelope usage; analyze at lines189-203 assigns usage only after successful decoding. Both independent mocked gateway probes recorded provider-reported 321 prompt/123 completion/444 total/12 cached for valid output, but four null usage fields when only role content became malformed JSON. Validate/retain safe envelope usage independently of content acceptance, including refusal, truncation and invalid-schema failures; keep genuinely absent/invalid usage unknown and never retain raw output.", "evidence": ["src/server/src/ai/gateway/index.ts", "src/server/src/ai/gateway/accounting.ts"]}, "kind": "finding request"},
    "review-finding-4.json": {"sha256": "5d4e07a70b52a8473f0fe9a3c4b281b4b2a1b26a350a246c308345e932718b03", "bytes": 946, "preserved": {"requirement": "REQ-REV-014; clear oversized-context explanation and manual fallback", "severity": "MEDIUM", "blocks": true, "owner": "ui", "reviewer": "independent-review", "description": "PatchRiskAssistant.tsx:77-80 discards the safe INPUT_LIMIT reason from a422 AI_UNAVAILABLE response and displays generic unavailability/try-again-later guidance. An independent in-memory TSX/JSDOM probe confirmed that exact feedback while manual/analyze controls remained enabled. Map allowlisted size-limit reasons to explicit guidance that the complete context exceeds AI limits and manual review remains available; preserve safe correlation references and test diff/total-context limit feedback. No component source was edited by the reviewer.", "evidence": ["src/client/src/features/reviewer/PatchRiskAssistant.tsx", "src/server/src/http.ts", "src/client/src/features/reviewer/PatchRiskAssistant.test.tsx"]}, "kind": "finding request"},
    "review-finding-5.json": {"sha256": "b51e7a829499bb0f65b38432552e237ad4f5e8ca90fbdea6c25aca957021a888", "bytes": 1126, "preserved": {"requirement": "REQ-REV-012; named suggestion-save/lifecycle concurrency evidence", "severity": "MEDIUM", "blocks": true, "owner": "reviewer-integration", "reviewer": "independent-review", "description": "The six ai-save-{new-revision,approval,drop-reclaim}-{event-first,save-first} cases at patch-risk.integration.ts:278-286 finish the first transaction before initiating the competing operation. Save-first also refreshes command coordinates before the lifecycle event. Passing these sequential cases does not prove lock-wait/stale-version behavior under contention. Initiate both operations with their original captured coordinates while one holds the relevant lock, prove the second is waiting, then release and assert allowed commits/conflicts plus atomic business/activity/notification outcomes. No production race failure is established; six matrix concurrency obligations remain unresolved despite green selectors.", "evidence": ["src/server/test/patch-risk.integration.ts", "logs/ngkhengyang/reviewer/2026-10-26-patch-risk-i3-implementation/inputs-summary.json#/entries/matrix-final-postgres.json"]}, "kind": "finding request"},
    "review-results.json": {"sha256": "8f51e46ebc6c993ef2d7702f6439afae8377ca742fac0520212fe1c6329af59d", "bytes": 7928, "preserved": {"reviewed_snapshot": "integrated-before-review", "base": "b8daea2dac771a0c372a01e4d0a23da4e44690e3", "decision": "changes_required", "source_unchanged": true, "findings": [{"origin": "SEC-CODE-001", "requirement": "REQ-REV-003/015; AI secret-exposure controls; NFR-PRV-001", "severity": "HIGH", "blocks": true, "owner": "gateway", "reviewer": "independent-review", "description": "Secret screening misses quoted JSON credential assignments, encrypted private-key markers and NFKC token representations. At src/server/src/ai/gateway/index.ts:28-31, the credential regex does not allow the JSON label's closing quote, encrypted PEM is omitted, and redaction uses original rather than normalized text. Both independent reviewers reproduced dispatch of synthetic examples with mocked Prisma/transport and no external calls. Reject high-confidence credential/private-key representations before attempts, consistently screen/redact normalized lower-confidence tokens without rewriting grounding IDs, and add adversarial cases across narrative, diff, criterion and evidence fields. Live provider mode remains disabled; no real credential disclosure is claimed.", "evidence": ["src/server/src/ai/gateway/index.ts", "src/server/test/ai-gateway.spec.ts"]}, {"origin": "SEC-CODE-002", "requirement": "REQ-REV-014; AI transport body/deadline/resource bounds", "severity": "MEDIUM", "blocks": true, "owner": "gateway", "reviewer": "independent-review", "description": "An oversized advertised Content-Length is rejected at transport.ts:41-42 before the body reader is acquired. Finally at lines61-63 clears timer/removes the deadline listener without aborting or cancelling the unread body. Both independent synthetic open-stream probes returned INVALID_OUTPUT while bodyCancelled=false and transportSignalAborted=false. Abort/cancel every early transport rejection with bounded cleanup; verify advertised and actual overflow, invalid UTF-8, and deadline during reads leave no live body. No real network call was made.", "evidence": ["src/server/src/ai/gateway/transport.ts", "src/server/test/ai-gateway.spec.ts"]}, {"origin": "SEC-CODE-003", "requirement": "NFR-OBS-001; NFR-RES-001; safe provider usage accounting", "severity": "MEDIUM", "blocks": true, "owner": "gateway", "reviewer": "independent-review", "description": "decode in gateway/index.ts:92-100 validates advisory content before returning envelope usage; analyze at lines189-203 assigns usage only after successful decoding. Both independent mocked gateway probes recorded provider-reported 321 prompt/123 completion/444 total/12 cached for valid output, but four null usage fields when only role content became malformed JSON. Validate/retain safe envelope usage independently of content acceptance, including refusal, truncation and invalid-schema failures; keep genuinely absent/invalid usage unknown and never retain raw output.", "evidence": ["src/server/src/ai/gateway/index.ts", "src/server/src/ai/gateway/accounting.ts"]}, {"origin": "REV-IR-001", "requirement": "REQ-REV-014; clear oversized-context explanation and manual fallback", "severity": "MEDIUM", "blocks": true, "owner": "ui", "reviewer": "independent-review", "description": "PatchRiskAssistant.tsx:77-80 discards the safe INPUT_LIMIT reason from a422 AI_UNAVAILABLE response and displays generic unavailability/try-again-later guidance. An independent in-memory TSX/JSDOM probe confirmed that exact feedback while manual/analyze controls remained enabled. Map allowlisted size-limit reasons to explicit guidance that the complete context exceeds AI limits and manual review remains available; preserve safe correlation references and test diff/total-context limit feedback. No component source was edited by the reviewer.", "evidence": ["src/client/src/features/reviewer/PatchRiskAssistant.tsx", "src/server/src/http.ts", "src/client/src/features/reviewer/PatchRiskAssistant.test.tsx"]}, {"origin": "REV-IR-002", "requirement": "REQ-REV-012; named suggestion-save/lifecycle concurrency evidence", "severity": "MEDIUM", "blocks": true, "owner": "reviewer-integration", "reviewer": "independent-review", "description": "The six ai-save-{new-revision,approval,drop-reclaim}-{event-first,save-first} cases at patch-risk.integration.ts:278-286 finish the first transaction before initiating the competing operation. Save-first also refreshes command coordinates before the lifecycle event. Passing these sequential cases does not prove lock-wait/stale-version behavior under contention. Initiate both operations with their original captured coordinates while one holds the relevant lock, prove the second is waiting, then release and assert allowed commits/conflicts plus atomic business/activity/notification outcomes. No production race failure is established; six matrix concurrency obligations remain unresolved despite green selectors.", "evidence": ["src/server/test/patch-risk.integration.ts", "logs/ngkhengyang/reviewer/2026-10-26-patch-risk-i3-implementation/inputs-summary.json#/entries/matrix-final-postgres.json"]}], "coverage": {"REQ-REV-003": "Implemented context/grounding controls supported; secret-screening finding remains open.", "REQ-REV-012": "Authorization, session and assignment-generation controls supported by inspection; six save-contention obligations lack actual concurrent evidence.", "REQ-REV-013": "Explicit human save/cancel, rollback and page-session state supported; real BFCache navigation/restoration not demonstrated.", "REQ-REV-014": "Server caps/manual fallback present; size-specific feedback and early transport cancellation fail.", "REQ-REV-015": "Own metadata and human-history separation supported; outbound secret screening and failed-response usage need correction."}, "checks": ["Both reviewers verified all36 source-manifest SHA256 entries unchanged.", "Implementation reviewer ran existing PatchRiskAssistant Vitest file:1 file,4 tests passed; these tests do not assert size-specific guidance.", "Implementation reviewer transpiled current TSX in memory under JSDOM/testing-library and supplied synthetic422 INPUT_LIMIT; exact generic feedback reproduced. Initial probe was invalidated by JSDOM initial pageshow; corrected probe awaited loading.", "Both reviewers independently ran trusted Node/ts-node stdin probes with synthetic mocked fetch/Prisma/transport to reproduce SEC-CODE001/002/003; no provider or database calls and no source/test files created.", "Security reviewer ran existing ai-gateway and ai-foundation suites:2 suites,11 tests passed; existing cases omit the reproduced variants. A preceding no-cache invocation had no captured completion and supplies no pass claim.", "No independent PostgreSQL/browser/build reruns were needed for these bounded reproductions; historical130 PostgreSQL/11 Chromium passes remain coordinator evidence, not fresh independent evidence."], "limitations": ["No production authorization bypass was established; the save-race finding is a verification gap.", "Live provider compatibility, tokenizer/retention, usefulness and latency remain unverified under OPEN-002; live operation stays disabled.", "Browser transient tests dispatch synthetic pagehide/pageshow then perform a real reload; actual browser BFCache restoration is not independently demonstrated.", "Operational records are physically pruned on a later gateway request and expired audit rows are hidden. No scheduler/caller for accounting.cleanup was found. The90-day logical-versus-guaranteed-physical-expiry interpretation remains unresolved; this is not a sixth confirmed blocker."]}, "kind": "review or closure decision"},
